# What NOT to upload to Vercel.
#
# ⚠️ VERCEL DOES NOT READ .gitignore. It reads this file, and otherwise skips
# only node_modules and .git — so every local-only build artifact was being
# uploaded with the source. That is invisible until one of them crosses the
# 100 MB per-file limit and the deploy fails with nothing but
# "File size limit exceeded (100 MB)", naming no file.
#
# Two of them cross it routinely: the packaged desktop installers, and the
# turbopack dev cache that `npm run dev` grows in .next.
#
# Everything listed here is either rebuilt on Vercel or belongs to a build that
# does not run there at all (the desktop app, the native bridge). Sources stay —
# only outputs are excluded.

# Rebuilt by Vercel; locally it also holds a multi-hundred-MB dev cache.
.next

# The desktop app: installers, the packaged .app, and its compiled main process.
dist-electron
dist-electron-apollo
electron/dist
electron/node_modules

# The native Beacon Bridge — built with cmake, never on Vercel.
bridge/build

# Local Python environment for the CLAP embeddings.
.venv-clap
